<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ihya al-Muluk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ihya al-Muluk is a Persian chronicle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sistan">Sistan</a> written in the early 17th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malik-shah-i">Malik Shah</a> Husayn Sistani, a member of the region's local ruling family. It traces the history of Sistan from legendary times to the author's own day, with particular detail on the Mihrabanid maliks who governed the province under Timurid and Safavid overlordship. It is a main source for the late medieval history of Sistan.</p></div>
